Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:05.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Imagine… every piece of iron on Earth suddenly vanished.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.80,0:00:07.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What would happen to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.60,0:00:11.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You are driving across a bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.40,0:00:13.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The radio is on.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.00,0:00:15.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Nothing feels wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.00,0:00:17.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.10,0:00:20.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your car falls apart around you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.30,0:00:23.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Steel is about ninety-eight percent iron.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.60,0:00:26.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The bridge has nothing left to hold it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.70,0:00:30.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Skyscrapers lose every steel beam.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.80,0:00:32.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But you won't see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.40,0:00:35.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The iron in your blood is gone too.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.20,0:00:38.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your blood can't carry oxygen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.60,0:00:41.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You black out in about ten seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.50,0:00:46.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Deep below, the iron core disappears.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.20,0:00:49.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Earth loses a third of its mass.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.00,0:00:53.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And the magnetic field that shields us… shuts off.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.30,0:00:55.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.90,0:00:59.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}That iron was never really from Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.00,0:01:04.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It was forged in exploding stars, long before our planet existed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.70,0:01:07.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.20,0:01:13.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your blood holds about four grams of star metal… enough for one small nail.
